{"id": "EUVD-2026-76533", "enisaUuid": "bdcffd42-091b-3c8e-ae7a-f4afd1d3953a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: mcp2221: validate report size in mcp2221_raw_event()\n\nmcp2221_raw_event() never validates the size of incoming HID reports.\nIn the MCP2221_I2C_GET_DATA path it trusts the device-supplied data[3]\nas the copy length without checking that 4 + data[3] bytes actually\nexist in the received report. A malicious or misbehaving USB device can\nsend a short report with a large data[3], causing the memcpy to read\npast the valid report data in the HID transfer buffer and leak\nuninitialized kernel memory back to userspace through the I2C/SMBus\nread path.\n\nAdd a minimum size check at entry and validate that the source range\nfits within the received report before the copy.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb38b1f149b7143355b37e86c841acf0076e5c2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2c67dc0e30c308647bbd9b9e5d69a44c9d2733d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fffcfa367072628c3144cca17d2a3c3c9e50c057", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1c508e8923911cb458234997e55b7a4b9aa066f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdc6a3af0dd734a326acdb7d6401a3b6a9f4f149", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/127de5919820f88a9d55e8371ad4ac49f625f4c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c18fb36708a97ff6772825cc087b6d537bbf0d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c9a6998c19503626c57a2267bf279e204113079"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89621", "GHSA-55hm-qvfp-55mj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07c3ea1a-4fdc-3302-bb8c-8247efe05ab2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "1251cf7e-62de-36a4-8a12-ab976ad7f933", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a95c21463d066060b0f66d65a75d45bb386ffb <c1c508e8923911cb458234997e55b7a4b9aa066f"}, {"id": "1639ceae-3bb9-3de2-bc14-7336ce38350e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a95c21463d066060b0f66d65a75d45bb386ffb <bdc6a3af0dd734a326acdb7d6401a3b6a9f4f149"}, {"id": "25e96e73-67b9-38df-9fdd-d5f4f2f599f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "3dc78c1e-6166-30a1-99be-4a75a85835a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "498ca8b3-d9d5-31b4-936d-7e7813f6dce4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4afa35e9-fc21-3f00-a855-8e3162a497eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5a28afa6-76ec-3122-99c2-10bf28554dc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a95c21463d066060b0f66d65a75d45bb386ffb <fffcfa367072628c3144cca17d2a3c3c9e50c057"}, {"id": "63d7c182-c700-30ae-9d64-fa940dc4789a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "688ee7e1-69f8-3028-be31-6f76f55269d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "80766dad-5366-3926-8b25-78db7df2befb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a95c21463d066060b0f66d65a75d45bb386ffb <cb38b1f149b7143355b37e86c841acf0076e5c2a"}, {"id": "81505d85-fdaa-39c1-a2a5-91ecfe1d8d92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a95c21463d066060b0f66d65a75d45bb386ffb <127de5919820f88a9d55e8371ad4ac49f625f4c5"}, {"id": "87f7623d-8f44-32df-bf01-b369e03e9dfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "8bde3361-3a14-3e05-90bf-2208dfa7ecf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67a